# Serena tool state
.serena/

# yash suite scratch, regenerated on every run. The tmp.NNN directories are
# per-test working copies the suite creates and cleans up itself - they were
# committed once because a run was in flight when third_party/ was added.
third_party/yash-tests/*.trs
third_party/yash-tests/tmp.*/

# Scratch a shell test leaves in the repo root. A snippet run with the repo as its
# working directory creates directories named after whatever it failed to expand -
# `for`, `in`, `do`, `;`, `[%s]` and friends turned up as twelve EMPTY directories,
# which `git status` cannot see, which is how they survived. Ignoring them is not
# enough on its own: prefer running probes under `tools/probe.py`, which works in a
# temporary directory for exactly this reason.
a:~root
tmp.h
